    "ordinaryInstallationAdmission": "rejected",
    "hostExecutionAuthorized": false,
    "isolatedMaliciousExecutionPerformedByReassessment": false,
    "reason": "The primary installation path is already bound to an unsigned replacement patch engine, while the package separately contains a malicious downloader MSI whose ordinary-path reachability remains unproven. Static rejection does not require inventing a causal edge between those branches."
  },
  "limitations": [
    "Absence of a literal nested-MSI reference in the wrapper action fields and outer MSI tables does not prove that no dynamic or data-dependent path can ever invoke it.",
    "Resolve.exe does not directly import intl.dll in the observed import table; the exact runtime module that loads the proxy DLL remains unproved by this reassessment.",
    "Historical CoreHubPro D0 receipts prove failed isolated attempts and clean closure, not successful malicious stage-2 activation.",
    "The historical stage-2 input bundle is no longer retained in the known Security state roots, so its acquisition provenance was not reconstructed in this reassessment."
  ],
  "nextResearchQuestions": [
    "Does ordinary execution of the exact wrapper in a no-NIC disposable Guest ever invoke the nested GetintoWAY MSI?",
